2026-11-07T06:33:13.5103531Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-07T06:33:13.5112341Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-07T06:33:13.5113302Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-07T06:33:13.5113826Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-07T06:33:13.5114186Z 
2026-11-07T06:33:13.5114501Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-07T06:33:13.5114927Z 
2026-11-07T06:33:13.5115275Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-07T06:33:13.5116100Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-07T06:33:13.5116331Z 
2026-11-07T06:33:13.5116453Z If you would like to
2026-11-07T06:33:13.5116737Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-07T06:33:13.5116954Z 
2026-11-07T06:33:13.5117421Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-07T06:33:13.5117842Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-07T06:33:13.5118011Z 
